{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/27756-setting-the-stage-trouble-with-new-systems","id":27756,"title":"Setting the Stage - Trouble with New Systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T21:40:34-08:00","id":27756,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Setting the Stage - Trouble with New Systems","content":"I've been trying to convince a few of my friends to give DtD (and by extention, the GMC rules) a try.<br /> <br /> Thery're having difficulty dealing with the seperaton of their covers from their character concept. And I can't exactly blame them on all counts. It's not like the two don't feed into each other at some points.<br /> <br /> So in order to put them at ease and increase my understanding, thereby allowing my group and I to set the stage for the latest NWoD game I am asking for your help.<br /> In the form of examples, preferably.<br /> <br /> Could someone help me illustrate the differences between the two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:33:11-08:00","id":27778,"title":"","content":"The demon is an Inhuman Thing. The Cover is the techno-mystical glasses, moustache, and &quot;Totally a human!&quot; T-shirt it wears to interact with reality in such a way that people don't run away screaming all the time (well, at least so they're not running away screaming because they see an Inhuman Thing. Plain old people can still be pretty scary).<br /> <br /> It's by no means a perfect analogy, as it doesn't cover nearly all the implications mechanically, but think of Men in Black, the Bug, and its 'Edgar Suit'. Horrible inhuman thing steals someone's identity and mainly draws suspiscion to itself by acting like itself instead of the identity it stole. That's a Soul Pact Cover being wasted by a demon not even trying to fit in. The other aliens hiding in human guise, including the tentacle monster Serleena and the underwear-model appearance she wraps around herself in MIB 2, are more like starting and patchwork covers. The aliens can still set off humans' suspicion by acting contrary to expectations - a talking pug, for example - but for the most part they try to blend in to the social roles they slink into and not draw the attention of people or Angels - that is, the MIB. To take advantage of their full not-human abilities, they need to give themselves away somehow (Compromise). They can shed one human guise for another, sometimes needfully after the old guise is worn out and discovered. But underneath it, they're still little green men, or giant bugs, or tentacle monsters with no concept of personal space or private orifices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:08:03-08:00","id":27795,"title":"","content":"I know that, but they are having trouble seperating the two. An example of the problem might help.<br /> <br /> One of my friends, (call him S for the sake of privacy), wants to create a tough biker character. That is fine, but that concept is good for the Cover. When asked about what kind of demon he want's to play, he said &quot;<i>One who enables this kind of concept, like Gangral goes with it.</i>&quot;<br /> Before anyone says anything, we did cover how any of Requeim's clans could be used for the concept. That's only part of the problem.<br /> <br /> The problem is the same as the one that made Promethean so unpalatible for the group.<br /> They see their characters as human's first. The idea that the character's personal identity is so heavily seperated from their humanity is hard for them to grasp.<br /> Just talking about the 'human suit' doesn't help. That said a couple of them twigged after I talked about Soul Pacts and compared them to a show they watched. (Supernatural, if you care. It was of the lines that 'Soul Pacts are like permanent poesession.')","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:42:55-08:00","id":27806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/27756-setting-the-stage-trouble-with-new-systems?p=27795#post27795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my friends, (call him S for the sake of privacy), wants to create a tough biker character. That is fine, but that concept is good for the Cover. When asked about what kind of demon he want's to play, he said &quot;<i>One who enables this kind of concept, like Gangral goes with it.</i>&quot;<br /> Before anyone says anything, we did cover how any of Requeim's clans could be used for the concept. That's only part of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I definitely think you guys are going about it the wrong way. The core character behind the Cover isn't human. He's not a &quot;tough biker&quot;, he's a fallen angel of the God-Machine. As such, he should think about what kind of Angel he was. What his mission was and how he Fell. Now, it's perfectly reasonable that the character's original mission involved posing as a &quot;tough biker&quot; and that's his original Cover. Heck, it's even possible that he identifies so strongly with the &quot;tough biker&quot; archetype that this is the kind of Cover that he now prefers. But honestly, any kind of Demon could have that kind of Cover. What your friend needs to do, is to decide what lead up to the character's Fall and why he identifies so strongly with this character type.<br /> <br /> If your group tends to see their characters as &quot;humans first&quot; it really might be difficult to get into the proper Demon frame of mind (then again, some Demons might identify so strongly with a particular Cover that they essentially become synonymous.) Maybe your players just aren't that interesting in the game's core premise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T01:45:06-08:00","id":27835,"title":"","content":"With some characters in <b>Demon</b>, saying something like &quot;I want to play a biker&quot; is less about who you want to play - like it is in normal games - and more about what you want to use as your favored tool, like &quot;I want to be a sniper&quot; or &quot;I want to play a face.&quot; The core of an Unchained are usually tied more into their motivations, goals, and conflicts than the aesthetics of a job or lifestyle; for most games things like &quot;biker&quot;, &quot;gang soldier&quot; or &quot;trophy wife&quot; give you guidelines for a core because you have to have lived your life in such a way to <i>become</i> these people. Saying &quot;I want to be a gang member&quot; usually assumes certain conditions you were in growing up, an environment you've lived in and are comfortable in, etc. Not so much with a demon who's claim to such a life is entirely artificial.<br /> <br /> That said, as Slaunyeh pointed out, for a lot of demons a Cover isn't just a body they wear like a cheap suit. It can be an expression of who they where - or who they like to be - and how they tend to approach problems. You can easily tie in something like that to the demon, it's just going to take a few more questions.<br /> <br /> For example, let's say you start off with &quot;I want to be a biker.&quot; My first two questions as ST would be &quot;has the character been a biker since it was an angel, or did it become one after he Fell?&quot; and &quot;what resources does being a biker bring a demon?&quot;<br /> <br /> If he's been a biker since he was an angel, then think about what type of mission from the God-Machine would warrant creating an angel as a biker. If it adopted the cover later, then reframe the question: what type of problems or obstacles did it decide could be best solved by becoming a biker, or what about being a biker drew it in enough that the cover became one of his top choices of personality, ethos, and modus operandi to approach the world in?<br /> <br /> Or here's another example: let's say I want to play a cop. How could this inform my character concept? Well, my character could have been built as a cop, as a Guardian to protect key Infrastructure or a Psychopomp using the position to arrange people, evidence and weaponry as befits the God-Machine's plans. If he chose to be a cop, it could be because he saw the position as a toolbox to use to influence and obtain both legal and illegal resources. It could be because he wants to protect and serve and a police officer is the best way for him to keep innocent people safe and keep the wicked off the streets. It could be a mix of all of these! Perhaps a very forceful demon with little compunction for the law met a dirty cop and found that the officer's methods and ethics compared nicely to his own and he also had access to high level contacts in both the city government and the local gangs and cartels. The demon decided it was a perfect fit, so he made arrangements, struck a deal with the dirty cop and soon enough walked the streets in his shoes, living his life.<br /> <br /> To cut an already too-long bit short, you can still approach the game with &quot;I want to be a biker&quot; so long as you're willing to come up with <i>why</i> you're a biker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 12-11-2013, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T01:54:01-08:00","id":27837,"title":"","content":"I actually think it's completely fine for a player to create a character based on the concept of the character's Cover. Seeing your character as &quot;human first&quot; is perfectly fine. That makes a statement about what kind of demon you are, though. You're one who's assimilated.<br /> <br /> A biker's interesting from that perspective, because that's someone who takes pride in being outside society. (I assume we're talking about a One Percenter here.) At the same time that they're taking themselves out of society, though, they're very in touch with their humanity. I think that would be a lot of fun to play out.<br /> <br /> <i>Demon</i>'s very much about human characters. &quot;Defected to the human race&quot; is right there in the pitch. The question is how they deal with their unique alienation; the fact that all of their emotional expressions are conscious, the fact that their lives are, at least initially, made out of lies.<br /> <br /> I didn't cite it in the book, but one of the inspirations behind <i>Demon</i>'s conflicted take on personal identity is Kurt Vonnegut's <i>Mother Night</i>. The novel follows a Nazi war criminal who's living undercover in New York. He has multiple identities: his everyday life, his Nazi past... and the fact that he was an American agent the whole time. Which, Vonnegut asks, is the real person? This is a question demons have to wrestle with. If I've taken on the role of a tough biker, how long do I have to act it out before that's really who I am? Or am I never really the person people see, but rather someone else, someone hidden?<br /> <br /> That's something we as humans all deal with, to a lesser or greater extent. We're so often wearing some kind of mask to interact with people. That can be a very solid mask, like when I was in the closet. Or it can be an almost invisible mask, as we try to live up to the standards set by our friends and family. If I'm a different person around my friends than around my family, who's the real me? It's a pretty elemental struggle, and one that I find interesting to explore in <i>Demon</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:20:16-08:00","id":27987,"title":"","content":"After playing a Sidereal for the past year and a half in a once (maybe twice) a week of Exalted, I think that I can easily play Demon with the simple divorced concept of Cover vs character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:54:54-08:00","id":28009,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, this should help alot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T15:49:49-08:00","id":28351,"title":"","content":"One way to explain it to them might be to talk about multiple Covers - a very desirable thing for any demon. Remind your player that he might be using his 'tough biker' cover one day, and his 'suburban housewife' one the next. For that matter, due to the need to maintain Cover, it's likely he'd use both in the same day. For the demon (assuming both have an equal Cover rating) both are equally valuable and valid parts of his life.<br /> <br /> Remind your player that his 'tough biker' cover may well become the casualty of the need to Go Loud in dire circumstances - at which point everything that it was will effectively be erased from his character's life and he will move on.<br /> <br /> In fact, one way to help your players conceptualise the concept might be to encourage them to take an additional Cover at character creation. Also, remind them that their character's attributes, skills and most if not all of their merits will be associated with their character, <i>not </i>their Cover (that's what Legend is for).<br /> <br /> Although it should be noted that this is one area I am struggling with somewhat. Conceptually, I think that most merits should be associated with the character, not the Cover, but it seems almost like 'free' merits in some sense, for those that are an integral part of a Cover (and therefore it seems a bit odd to be constantly rolling Legend for). Take the aforementioned example - in one sense you 'should' buy 2 Resources for the biker and 3 Resources for the suburban housewife, becuase you do after all have access to those...but by the same token these covers are both 'disposable', plus the need to buy merit dots for both your character and their Cover is just impossible, expenditure-wise. My inclination is to treat Covers as if they had all of the appropriate merits associated with them, but remembering that none of those are protected by the sanctity of merits principle.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'd appreciate some designer feedback on that last point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1606-psychochink","name":"Psychochink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T15:51:28-08:00","id":28352,"title":"","content":"On an unrelated note, I am very taken with the idea of playing a character whose primary Cover is that of a hit man, spy or similar - a Cover with a cover of their own to maintain. Layers within layers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1606-psychochink","name":"Psychochink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:12:38-08:00","id":28403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psychochink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/27756-setting-the-stage-trouble-with-new-systems?p=28351#post28351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind your player that his 'tough biker' cover may well become the casualty of the need to Go Loud in dire circumstances - at which point everything that it was will effectively be erased from his character's life and he will move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, of course, not necessarily move on quietly. I have a character who is terribly attached to her initial cover - some demons would say unhealthily, probably. One of the several pressing priorities she'll be juggling is working to establish a second cover quickly. She doesn't particularly care what that cover ends up being, she just wants to be sure that, if she gets into a situation where it's necessary to Go Loud (and as a Destroyer Saboteur... yeah, not unlikely), she can cast that one aside instead. Of course, if she's not prepared, she might get caught in a dire situation in her 'good' Cover...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T20:02:44-08:00","id":28485,"title":"","content":"For real though, players having trouble separating the two if anything lends itself well to Demon. Make that the theme you've got going on, or at least explore it more. Well, after at least they start catching on to how it works I suppose, or it could be a weird as fuck game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1254-grieck","name":"grieck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1254_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T20:03:15-08:00","id":28486,"title":"","content":"Duly noted, Psychochink. Reminding them that they can have more than one Cover and that they may need to Go Loud at some point should keep them from getting a little too myopic about it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of merits...one that I'm confused about is Professional Training. It's the sort of thing that makes more sense for a Cover to have, but it appears to be based on the mental processes, (which are inheirent), needed for that job, (past the first dot anyway). Any advice on how to deal with splitting merits between Cover and Demon?<br /> <br /> Edit:@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1254-grieck\">grieck: </a></b>I absolutely agree and I am looking forward to it. But I want them to be aware of the possiblities from the begining, just in case. squidheadjax's character's story would be very different if she didn't comprehend what it means to Go Loud. Having to watch all the inter-character development disappear in the event you have to Go Loud will be hard enough for my group; when it sinks in that you've more than killed that Cover there is going to be tears.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to get them a bit more aware to the idea <i>now</i>, rather than wait until it happens. A little meta-gamey I know, but funnily enough I don't like to see my friends in real pain. And yes I am aware this would be less of an issue if they weren't so attached to their characters, but the games wouldn't be as much fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  ninja'd while posting 12-11-2013, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T21:10:36-08:00","id":28520,"title":"","content":"Alternately, I'd encourage the player to look into maintaining multiple &quot;tough biker&quot; covers. Each with ties to different gangs. <br /> <br /> So one cover that is your stereotypical one percenter with ties to the aryan brotherhood. And then another with ties to Mexican drug cartels. And then later a third that's in with the Korean street racers. So the Demon consistently self-identifies as a &quot;tough biker&quot;, but what exactly that means might vary from cover to cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}